**Convention 8.3 (separate charges and recoverable boundary data).**
The public graph, orientation, slot order, scaffold, membership tables
and decoder tables are installed source-independent data. Their
generation and size, preparation work/control and temporary storage,
post-request workspace, address construction, final predictor size,
authentic-count representation, lawful entry, authentication, handoff,
isolation and physical time remain separate resources. Only the factor
alone has the credited bit bound
$\lceil\log_2(2D+1)\rceil+1$, from $0\le b\le2D$ and
$c\in\{0,1\}$. This is not a bound on all predictor machinery.
The construction neither minimizes preparation cost nor preserves the
acquisition cost of an arbitrary old competitor.

The boundary observer recovers exactly the requested temporal factor
and hence its authentic-count trajectory from the complete acquired
name plus at most one actual reply. Conversely that trajectory
determines the factor's first branch count and alpha-stage flag.
This limited mutual recovery supplies no whole-source, hidden-age,
unseen-history or physical space-time recovery. The analytical seed
assignment, kernel component and syndrome are not supplied to the
reader. The paid interface services are not inferred physical operations.

